## {{lb|en|obsolete|figurative}} A [[small#Adjective|small]] [[piece#Noun|piece]]; a [[fragment#Noun|fragment]].
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Much Ado About Nothing Q|act=II|scene=iii|sig=D2|page=30|passage=O ſhe tore the letter into a thouſand '''halfpence''', raild at her ſelf, that ſhe ſhould be ſo immodeſt to vvrite, to one that ſhe knevv vvould flout her, {{...}}}}

====Usage notes====
Regarding {{senseno|en|UK coin}} (“discontinued English (later British) coin”), between 1971 when the currency of the United Kingdom was decimalized, and 1984 when the halfpenny coin was demonetized, the coin was often written as {{m|en|half penny}} and pronounced {{IPAchar|/ˌhɑːfˈpɛni/|a=RP|/ˌhæfˈpɛni/|a2=GA}}. Now, when it is necessary to refer to the amount of money, it is generally written ''half a penny''.<ref name="OED"/>

